&lt;li&gt;12+ years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Electrical or Computer Engineering or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player with strong organization and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with schematic design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing board bring-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing schematic reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently under tight deadlines with minimal supervision, delivering quality results in fast-paced environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing checklists and procedures for developed designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing technical drawings and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with power circuit design and implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with lab equipment (DMM, O-Scope, Power Supply, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be authorized to work in the United States&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schematic and layout design in Altium&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing PDN analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with differential pair routing and debugging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in soldering&lt;/li&gt;
